menu "Pharos board"

config PHAROS_HAS_VENDOR_BSP
    bool "Drive the real Waveshare BSP (enable at hardware bring-up)"
    default n
    help
        Off by default: the firmware builds and links for ESP32-S3 with a
        simulated board, which is what CI verifies and what lets the runtime
        be exercised over serial before the panel is driven.

        Turn this on at milestone M1, when you have the board and can confirm
        the Waveshare component's bsp_* function names against the installed
        version. Enabling it also requires adding the vendor component to the
        REQUIRES list in components/pharos_bsp/CMakeLists.txt.

endmenu
